         "DBP" : {
            "PMID_claude_generated" : [
               "39107824"
            ],
            "anno" : "Single-stranded DNA-binding protein",
            "comment" : "Siadenovirus DBP is spliced: turkey hemorrhagic enteritis virus (THEV, Virginia avirulent strain) CDS starts at 18186 with a 10-residue exon 1, donor 18159, a 72-nt intron, acceptor 18087, giving a 380-aa protein (PMID 39107824, Tables 2 and S3; verified on AY849321: ATG, GT..AG, 380 aa). The previous PSSM called only the exon-2 portion (336-350 aa). Extended to other siadenoviruses by aligning the donor and acceptor regions to the THEV anchor; because exon 1 is too short to align as protein it was located from the acceptor side and, where needed, by searching for the ATG..GT exon 1 that keeps exon 2 in frame and best matches the THEV exon-1 peptide (unique best only). Every distinct product was translated and aligned with the anchor product to confirm exon 2 is in frame. Covers 42 of 69 module genomes; 10 of the misses are partial THEV assemblies (23.8 kb) lacking the region. 17 unique references, products 368-382 aa; min_len = 0.95 x shortest. Jim chose splice over the exon-2 PSSM (13 Nov 2026).",
